# @slayzone/server — what's left

Companion to artifact `e684e7d4 server-extraction-audit.md`. Same items, table form.

## Open work

| ID | Category | Severity | Effort | Item | Fix |
|----|----------|----------|--------|------|-----|
| A1 | Production blocker | HIGH | ~1d | No authentication on remote tRPC | Add auth middleware to `wsLink` (Bearer token in URL or upgrade headers). Validate on server. Store auth token alongside `remote_server_url` in settings. Critical before any non-localhost deployment. |
| A2 | Production blocker | HIGH | ~0.5d | No fallback if remote unreachable post-relaunch | `RemoteConfigScreen` polls `/health` with timeout (10s); auto-fall-back to local mode if remote is down. Today user is stuck on the config screen with only a manual mode revert. |
| A3 | Production blocker | MEDIUM | TBD | Integration pollers (Linear, GitHub) skipped in remote mode | Architectural decision: either move pollers into `@slayzone/server` so the remote runs them, or document remote mode disables external sync. See `apps/app/src/main/index.ts:1760-1766`. |
| B1 | Polish | LOW | ~2h | Feedback ops still in `appDeps` | 6 pure DB ops at `apps/app/src/main/index.ts:1343-1354`. Extract to `packages/domains/feedback/src/server/` + add `feedbackRouter` to transport. |
| B2 | Polish | LOW | ~3h | Pre-boot settings reads in Electron host | `apps/app/src/main/index.ts:962-1000` reads onboarding/theme/CLI-migration settings via raw `db.prepare(...)` BEFORE the embedded server boots. Defer reads until post-boot, or cache + sync from server when ready. |
| B3 | Polish | DEFERRED | ~8h | Backup + export/import are Electron-coupled | Pure file I/O ops in `appDeps` (`backupList`, `backupCreate`, `exportAll`, `exportProject`, `importBundle`). Extract pure logic to `@slayzone/backup` package; keep file dialogs in `appDeps`. Lets CLI users get backups too. |
| C1 | Architecture decision | OPEN | n/a | Single-user vs multi-user remote | Never explicitly decided. Auth strategy hinges on this. Single-user → simple Bearer token. Multi-user → per-user isolation in `@slayzone/server`. |
| C2 | Architecture decision | LOW | ~1d | Schema-version drift mid-upload | Schema match checked only at preflight (`local-export.ts:99-103`), not per-chunk. Edge case: network failure + version skew during retry could silently corrupt. Fix: include `user_version` in every chunk manifest + validate per-chunk on commit. |
| C3 | Architecture decision | DEFERRED | ~2d | No upload resumability | Wizard says "don't close SlayZone" but a process death mid-upload leaves dirty remote state, no GC, no resume token. Server returns resumable upload ID from preflight; client checkpoints chunk offset; remote GCs uploads stale > 1h. Only matters at scale. |

## Recommended path to "remote-mode shippable"

| Order | Item | Effort | Cumulative |
|-------|------|--------|------------|
| 1 | A1 — Auth headers in `wsLink` + remote validation | 1d | 1d |
| 2 | A2 — `RemoteConfigScreen` timeout + auto-fallback | 0.5d | 1.5d |
| 3 | Doc — Single-user constraint + firewall guidance | 0.25d | 1.75d |
| 4 | B1 — Extract feedback to a domain | 0.25d | 2d |
| 5 | CI — End-to-end local→remote migration test | 1d | 3d |

**Total: ~3 days to ship-able remote mode.**

Defer until later: B3 (backup to server, separate value), C3 (resumability, only matters at scale), A3 + C1 (architectural decisions, post-shippable).
